 the writing gig. (event_time: 2022-03-24T13:43:00Z)\n  - Nate hopes that people will love Joanna's screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Nate asked Joanna how she feels now that the screenplay is finished. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna uses writing as a way to express her feelings (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna has been working on a screenplay. (event_time: 2022-05-02T11:54:00Z)\n  - Joanna's screenplay might be loved by a director. (event_time: 2022-02-07T09:27:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - film festivals: Joanna submitted her screenplay to a film festival, feeling relief, excitement, and worry while hoping a producer or director selects it for the big screen.\n  - hope: Joanna experiences a tug-of-war of hope and doubt after wrapping up her second script, feeling a mix of relief and anxiety about future recognition.\n  - doubt: Joanna expressed a 'tug-of-war of hope and doubt' after finishing her second script, feeling a mix of excitement and terror about her work getting noticed.\n  - positive feedback: Joanna hopes finishing her first screenplay will lead to positive feedback and new opportunities.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - new things: Joanna submitted a screenplay to a film contest and mentioned that people love it when she makes them new things.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her feelings, act as